WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.266 --> 00:00:01.434 align:start size:94% position:6%
-We actually saw each other
this morning.

00:00:01.434 --> 00:00:03.370
NBC upfronts for this morning --
for those who don't know,

00:00:03.370 --> 00:00:07.207 align:start size:94% position:6%
that's where basically NBC
comes up to advertisers

00:00:07.207 --> 00:00:08.074 line:92%
and talks about their shows.

00:00:08.074 --> 00:00:09.776 align:start size:94% position:6%
Needless to say, they talked
a lot about "This Is Us,"

00:00:09.776 --> 00:00:11.311 align:start size:94% position:6%
a show they're very proud of.
-Yeah.

00:00:11.311 --> 00:00:13.079 align:start size:94% position:6%
-We have to be there.
We're contractually obligated.

00:00:13.079 --> 00:00:17.250
-It is the one thing we have to
be at, per our contracts.

00:00:17.250 --> 00:00:19.285 align:start size:94% position:6%
But it's -- it's fun?
-It's not bad.

00:00:19.285 --> 00:00:20.720 align:start size:94% position:6%
-It's not bad.
Like, this is the fun part.

00:00:20.720 --> 00:00:23.923 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, this is -- I'm glad.
You were in New York for that.

00:00:23.923 --> 00:00:25.859 align:start size:94% position:6%
But the one thing
that's nice is,

00:00:25.859 --> 00:00:27.761 align:start size:94% position:6%
you guys genuinely seem to be
a cast that gets along.

00:00:27.761 --> 00:00:29.129
And you guys haven't seen
each other for a while,

00:00:29.129 --> 00:00:30.530
because you wrapped, obviously,
way back.

00:00:30.530 --> 00:00:31.564 align:start size:94% position:6%
Was it nice to see everybody
today?

00:00:31.564 --> 00:00:33.400
-It was fun, but it was also --
it was one of those things

00:00:33.400 --> 00:00:35.835 align:start size:94% position:6%
where it's kind of like --
even like --

00:00:35.835 --> 00:00:38.071 align:start size:94% position:6%
I'm on the show,
but I'm kind of dead.

00:00:38.071 --> 00:00:39.105 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, yeah, yeah.
[ Laughter ]

00:00:39.105 --> 00:00:42.675 align:start size:94% position:6%
-So it's like, um, I'm kind of
in my own world with Mandy.

00:00:42.675 --> 00:00:44.944 size:81% position:41%
So when I see, like,
the rest of everybody,

00:00:44.944 --> 00:00:45.712 line:92%
I kind of feel like, "Man,

00:00:45.712 --> 00:00:47.047 size:75% position:38%
I'm not really in on
some of the jokes."

00:00:47.047 --> 00:00:48.114 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Oh, yeah, that's true!
-A little bit.

00:00:48.114 --> 00:00:50.350 size:84% position:42%
-Yeah, unless there are
some ghost episodes,

00:00:50.350 --> 00:00:51.451 align:start size:94% position:6%
you don't ever
work with those people.

00:00:51.451 --> 00:00:54.154 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I know. Or, you know,
they're on drugs or mushrooms.

00:00:54.154 --> 00:00:55.688 size:75% position:38%
-[ Laughing ] Right.
-Or, like, you know,

00:00:55.688 --> 00:00:58.058
hitting the bottle really hard.
Those are the times, yeah.

00:00:58.058 --> 00:00:59.526 align:start size:94% position:6%
-That could work out, yeah.
-Exactly.

00:00:59.526 --> 00:01:02.595 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You've been on some other
sort of cult shows --

00:01:02.595 --> 00:01:04.097 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Gilmore Girls," "Heroes."
-Yeah.

00:01:04.097 --> 00:01:05.832 size:84% position:42% line:92%
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:05.832 --> 00:01:09.369 align:start size:94% position:6%
-What is -- Have you
seen a difference

00:01:09.369 --> 00:01:12.138
between the kind of people that
approached you for those shows

00:01:12.138 --> 00:01:14.774
and the kind of people who
approach you about "This Is Us"?

00:01:14.774 --> 00:01:16.109 align:start size:94% position:6%
-"Gilmore Girls" was like,
"Hey!" --

00:01:16.109 --> 00:01:17.377 align:start size:94% position:6%
a lot of moms and daughters,
you know,

00:01:17.377 --> 00:01:18.978 align:start size:94% position:6%
that say they're best friends.
-That tracks.

00:01:18.978 --> 00:01:21.514
-And then occasionally, there'd
be, like, one dude

00:01:21.514 --> 00:01:23.550 line:92%
who's like, "Oh, man. Jess?"

00:01:23.550 --> 00:01:24.584 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:01:24.584 --> 00:01:26.319 line:92%
And then "Heroes" was, you know,

00:01:26.319 --> 00:01:27.787 align:start size:94% position:6%
the person
that's into comic books.

00:01:27.787 --> 00:01:29.289 align:start size:94% position:6%
This is everyone.
-Yeah.

00:01:29.289 --> 00:01:31.724 size:88% position:44%
-And it's so encouraging
that a show like this --

00:01:31.724 --> 00:01:35.161 align:start size:94% position:6%
it's so encouraging
that, like, the arts

00:01:35.161 --> 00:01:38.465
can still make an impact
on a wide group of people.

00:01:38.465 --> 00:01:42.502
I mean, young, old, every
ethnicity, every -- everything.

00:01:42.502 --> 00:01:43.670 align:start size:94% position:6%
It's just, people
watch the show.

00:01:43.670 --> 00:01:46.940
And they're talking about it
and it's important to them

00:01:46.940 --> 00:01:48.041 line:92%
and it's part of the good.

00:01:48.041 --> 00:01:50.143
It's part of the good that is
out in the world right now.

00:01:50.143 --> 00:01:53.613 align:start size:94% position:6%
It's inspiring hope.
It's inspiring communication.

00:01:53.613 --> 00:01:54.814 align:start size:94% position:6%
I don't know, inclusion.
A lot of things

00:01:54.814 --> 00:01:56.249 align:start size:94% position:6%
that some places are missing
right now.

00:01:56.249 --> 00:01:57.851 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Well, that's really nice
you guys do that.

00:01:57.851 --> 00:01:59.052 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:59.052 --> 00:02:02.155 align:start size:94% position:6%
-One of the things, obviously,
people were talking about,

00:02:02.155 --> 00:02:06.659
from the beginning of the show,
was how Jack was going to die.

00:02:06.659 --> 00:02:07.360 size:81% position:41% line:92%
-Of course, of course.

00:02:07.360 --> 00:02:09.929 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And it turned out
it was a slow cooker.

00:02:09.929 --> 00:02:10.563 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Light laughter ]

00:02:10.563 --> 00:02:14.234 size:75% position:38%
-I think it was like
a slow-cooker combo

00:02:14.234 --> 00:02:16.369 align:start size:94% position:6%
with, like, you know,
the neighbor dropping it off

00:02:16.369 --> 00:02:18.371 size:84% position:42%
and, like, no batteries
in the smoke detector.

00:02:18.371 --> 00:02:20.006 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
A lot of different things.

00:02:20.006 --> 00:02:21.875 align:start size:94% position:6%
-It's Colonel Mustard
in the library.

00:02:21.875 --> 00:02:24.177 align:start size:94% position:6%
You really don't know
if that's him.

00:02:24.177 --> 00:02:25.845 line:92%
-There is now a decal out

00:02:25.845 --> 00:02:28.214 align:start size:94% position:6%
that people have been putting
on their slow cookers.

00:02:28.214 --> 00:02:29.749 align:start size:94% position:6%
Have you seen this?
-I have seen it.

00:02:29.749 --> 00:02:32.252
It says, like,
"Please unplug me. Love, Jack."

00:02:32.252 --> 00:02:33.553 align:start size:94% position:6%
-[ Laughing ] Yeah.
[ Laughter ]

00:02:33.553 --> 00:02:35.421 line:92%
-Yeah, I know. Which is clever.

00:02:35.421 --> 00:02:36.990 align:start size:94% position:6%
It's like, "Man, that person,
hopefully,

00:02:36.990 --> 00:02:38.791 align:start size:94% position:6%
they can make a lot of change
off of that."

00:02:38.791 --> 00:02:39.459 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-Yeah.

00:02:39.459 --> 00:02:40.760 align:start size:94% position:6%
-It would be nice for them.
And, hopefully,

00:02:40.760 --> 00:02:42.595 align:start size:94% position:6%
they use that money
for good, as well, you know?

00:02:42.595 --> 00:02:45.532
-Totally.
Donate it, donate it, donate it.

00:02:45.532 --> 00:02:46.766 align:start size:94% position:6%
Please, please.
-Yeah, exactly.

00:02:46.766 --> 00:02:48.735 align:start size:94% position:6%
-One of the things
I love about the show

00:02:48.735 --> 00:02:51.437 align:start size:94% position:6%
is based on the fact that I am
a huge Steelers fan.

00:02:51.437 --> 00:02:55.275 align:start size:94% position:6%
This is a show about Steelers.
This is a Steelers family.

00:02:55.275 --> 00:02:56.876 align:start size:94% position:6%
-This is a Steelers family,
100%.

00:02:56.876 --> 00:02:58.611 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And has the --
And it sounds like

00:02:58.611 --> 00:03:01.047
the actual Steelers family
has been very good to you guys.

00:03:01.047 --> 00:03:03.783
They've embraced the idea.
-The Rooneys are awesome.

00:03:03.783 --> 00:03:04.851 line:92%
Everyone in the organization

00:03:04.851 --> 00:03:07.854 align:start size:94% position:6%
has really embraced
our embracing of them.

00:03:07.854 --> 00:03:10.190 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I got to admit, you know,
before the show,

00:03:10.190 --> 00:03:12.258 align:start size:94% position:6%
I didn't know a whole lot
about the Steelers.

00:03:12.258 --> 00:03:12.926 size:88% position:44% line:92%
I knew they were kind of

00:03:12.926 --> 00:03:14.260 size:88% position:44%
one of the dynasty teams
that have been around.

00:03:14.260 --> 00:03:18.031
They have this magical history,
and I knew some awesome players,

00:03:18.031 --> 00:03:22.669 align:start size:94% position:6%
you know, past and present.
And so I'm a new fan.

00:03:22.669 --> 00:03:24.737 align:start size:94% position:6%
But that doesn't make me
any less of a fan.

00:03:24.737 --> 00:03:26.506 align:start size:94% position:6%
I'm still excited
about the Steelers.

00:03:26.506 --> 00:03:28.708
And when they were marching
up toward that Super Bowl,

00:03:28.708 --> 00:03:30.677
like, "Please, please, please.
Come on, that would be great."

00:03:30.677 --> 00:03:31.978
-It would be great for the show.
Yeah.

00:03:31.978 --> 00:03:33.580 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]
-We actually -- We actually --

00:03:33.580 --> 00:03:35.114 align:start size:94% position:6%
-It'd be great for the show.
-If you watch the episode

00:03:35.114 --> 00:03:36.549 align:start size:94% position:6%
where -- I know,
it would be amazing!

00:03:36.549 --> 00:03:39.953 align:start size:94% position:6%
If you watch the episode
where my character --

00:03:39.953 --> 00:03:41.454 align:start size:94% position:6%
yeah, where he dies
in the Super Bowl --

00:03:41.454 --> 00:03:44.057 align:start size:94% position:6%
we had actual real
Super Bowl footage in there.

00:03:44.057 --> 00:03:45.291 line:92%
So had it been the Steelers,

00:03:45.291 --> 00:03:46.693 align:start size:94% position:6%
we would have had,
in the present day,

00:03:46.693 --> 00:03:49.495 align:start size:94% position:6%
Steelers actual footage
in that episode.

00:03:49.495 --> 00:03:50.630 align:start size:94% position:6%
-That's fantastic.
-It was crazy.

00:03:50.630 --> 00:03:52.365 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And I'm always a fan,
because, otherwise,

00:03:52.365 --> 00:03:54.801 align:start size:94% position:6%
I just have to watch
old Super Bowls on YouTube.

00:03:54.801 --> 00:03:56.769 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Like, "oh, yeah, that was --"
Yeah, yeah, yeah.

00:03:56.769 --> 00:03:59.172
-So, for me to be able to watch
something with my wife

00:03:59.172 --> 00:04:00.773 align:start size:94% position:6%
where I also see
old Super Bowl footage,

00:04:00.773 --> 00:04:02.308 align:start size:94% position:6%
that's like a double bonus.
-Right? Yeah.

00:04:02.308 --> 00:04:03.977 align:start size:94% position:6%
She's like, "Honey,
we've already seen

00:04:03.977 --> 00:04:06.045 align:start size:94% position:6%
the Bradshaw victory."
-"Come on!

00:04:06.045 --> 00:04:06.879 line:92%
Come on over to the computer.

00:04:06.879 --> 00:04:08.715 align:start size:94% position:6%
Let's watch
some old grainy YouTubes."

00:04:08.715 --> 00:04:09.849 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]
-Totally.

00:04:09.849 --> 00:04:12.485 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Next -- Is it correct,
the next season,

00:04:12.485 --> 00:04:14.887
you're going to sort of explore
the fact that Jack --

00:04:14.887 --> 00:04:16.189 align:start size:94% position:6%
a Vietnam vet?
-Yes.

00:04:16.189 --> 00:04:19.025 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And that was true of
your father in real life.

00:04:19.025 --> 00:04:21.261 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, my dad's
a two-tour Vietnam vet.

00:04:21.261 --> 00:04:23.396 align:start size:94% position:6%
And you know, when I was --
Yeah.

00:04:23.396 --> 00:04:25.999 size:84% position:42% line:92%
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:25.999 --> 00:04:28.868 line:92%
When I was younger, you know,

00:04:28.868 --> 00:04:30.403 size:84% position:42%
I'd always ask my dad
stories and everything.

00:04:30.403 --> 00:04:34.274
And he was very candid with me,
his son, about his experience.

00:04:34.274 --> 00:04:36.209 size:88% position:44% line:92%
And when I knew that was

00:04:36.209 --> 00:04:39.178 align:start size:94% position:6%
the road we were going to
travel on for Jack,

00:04:39.178 --> 00:04:40.947 size:78% position:39% line:92%
I wanted to know more

00:04:40.947 --> 00:04:43.082 align:start size:94% position:6%
the feeling,
like, the understanding,

00:04:43.082 --> 00:04:45.018 size:81% position:41%
like, what it is to be
in the theater of war

00:04:45.018 --> 00:04:47.520 align:start size:94% position:6%
and what you take
from that experience

00:04:47.520 --> 00:04:48.821 align:start size:94% position:6%
and what you try
and leave behind

00:04:48.821 --> 00:04:50.990 align:start size:94% position:6%
in a situation
that's so horrible.

00:04:50.990 --> 00:04:52.892 align:start size:94% position:6%
I mean, I've got
a lot of friends, even,

00:04:52.892 --> 00:04:57.363 line:92%
that are present day, in uniform

00:04:57.363 --> 00:05:00.366 align:start size:94% position:6%
or, you know, combat veterans,
combat wounded veterans.

00:05:00.366 --> 00:05:02.835 align:start size:94% position:6%
Like, I've got great friends
that are serving.

00:05:02.835 --> 00:05:03.803 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And you've gone over.
-Yeah.

00:05:03.803 --> 00:05:06.239
-You've visited troops overseas.
What's that experience like?

00:05:06.239 --> 00:05:07.373 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Heavy.
-Yeah.

00:05:07.373 --> 00:05:08.474 align:start size:94% position:6%
-It's really heavy.
And you know what?

00:05:08.474 --> 00:05:11.344
The one thing that I really
took from it, when I got home --

00:05:11.344 --> 00:05:14.681 align:start size:94% position:6%
I mean, we were in Iraq,
Afghanistan, Bahrain,

00:05:14.681 --> 00:05:16.949 align:start size:94% position:6%
you know,
different operating bases.

00:05:16.949 --> 00:05:18.484 align:start size:94% position:6%
You know, flying
in Chinooks and Black Hawks

00:05:18.484 --> 00:05:20.086 align:start size:94% position:6%
to places that no one's
every heard of.

00:05:20.086 --> 00:05:24.590 align:start size:94% position:6%
And you're experiencing
this visceral thing

00:05:24.590 --> 00:05:27.327 align:start size:94% position:6%
and you're seeing
the beat-up faces

00:05:27.327 --> 00:05:29.562 align:start size:94% position:6%
of these soldiers and sailors
and airmen and Marines.

00:05:29.562 --> 00:05:32.965 align:start size:94% position:6%
And you get home,
and no one else that's at home

00:05:32.965 --> 00:05:35.068 align:start size:94% position:6%
really remembers
that there's a war

00:05:35.068 --> 00:05:36.903 align:start size:94% position:6%
and there are Americans
in other countries

00:05:36.903 --> 00:05:39.038
that are coming together to,
hopefully, do something good.

00:05:39.038 --> 00:05:40.873 align:start size:94% position:6%
It's just -- It was
one of those things

00:05:40.873 --> 00:05:42.241 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
where I wanted to,

00:05:42.241 --> 00:05:44.377 size:75% position:38%
in the duty of being
an American citizen,

00:05:44.377 --> 00:05:46.212 align:start size:94% position:6%
as well kind of
honoring my father

00:05:46.212 --> 00:05:47.914 align:start size:94% position:6%
and what his generation
experienced,

00:05:47.914 --> 00:05:50.216 size:78% position:39%
acknowledge soldiers
that are coming home,

00:05:50.216 --> 00:05:52.719 line:92%
and be like, "Hey, we see you.

00:05:52.719 --> 00:05:53.953 size:88% position:44% line:92%
Let's see what we can do

00:05:53.953 --> 00:05:55.922 align:start size:94% position:6%
to, like, kind of
plug you back into society

00:05:55.922 --> 00:05:57.056 align:start size:94% position:6%
and do something bigger
for you."

00:05:57.056 --> 00:05:58.424 align:start size:94% position:6%
-That's wonderful.
I look forward to that.

00:05:58.424 --> 00:05:59.659 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Cheers and applause ]
-Yeah.

00:05:59.659 --> 00:06:01.260 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Last thing I want to
ask you about --

00:06:01.260 --> 00:06:05.131 size:88% position:44%
you -- true that you are
a motorcycle aficionado?

00:06:05.131 --> 00:06:05.665 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Yeah.

00:06:05.665 --> 00:06:07.367 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You drive them around L.A.?
-I do.

00:06:07.367 --> 00:06:09.602 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Do people ever recognize you,
or are you helmeted up?

00:06:09.602 --> 00:06:11.437 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Not so much.
I'm fully helmeted up.

00:06:11.437 --> 00:06:13.573 align:start size:94% position:6%
I mean, that's the good thing
about motorcycles.

00:06:13.573 --> 00:06:15.074 align:start size:94% position:6%
You kind of get
in and out of traffic,

00:06:15.074 --> 00:06:16.409 align:start size:94% position:6%
park wherever you want.
-Yep.

00:06:16.409 --> 00:06:19.779 align:start size:94% position:6%
And is it true that you know
motorcycles so well

00:06:19.779 --> 00:06:23.282 align:start size:94% position:6%
that you can tell a motorcycle
by -- from sound alone?

00:06:23.282 --> 00:06:24.217 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Sometimes.
-Yeah.

00:06:24.217 --> 00:06:26.018 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I was actually --
I was doing an interview

00:06:26.018 --> 00:06:29.288 align:start size:94% position:6%
for the upfront presentation
up in Vancouver.

00:06:29.288 --> 00:06:31.057 align:start size:94% position:6%
That was a weird train.
-Yeah.

00:06:31.057 --> 00:06:33.292 size:75% position:38%
-But I was up there,
and the sound guy,

00:06:33.292 --> 00:06:36.229 size:84% position:42%
he had to stop the take
or stop the interview

00:06:36.229 --> 00:06:38.297 align:start size:94% position:6%
because he goes, "Oh, sorry,
motorcycle is going by."

00:06:38.297 --> 00:06:39.232 line:92%
I'm like, "Yeah, that was, like,

00:06:39.232 --> 00:06:43.669
'88 Road Glide Special
with extra piping, yeah."

00:06:43.669 --> 00:06:45.271
And then like two or three bikes
went by.

00:06:45.271 --> 00:06:46.839
I'm like, "That was a Triumph."
-Wow!

00:06:46.839 --> 00:06:48.975 align:start size:94% position:6%
-So you're like a
motorcycle Rain Man.

00:06:48.975 --> 00:06:50.309 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Kind of. Yeah, I know.
[ Laughter ]

00:06:50.309 --> 00:06:53.980
-That is a skill that's
going to make you no, no money.

00:06:53.980 --> 00:06:56.482
-None at all.
There's no fun with that at all.

00:06:56.482 --> 00:06:57.417 line:92%
-There's no... [ Laughs ]

00:06:57.417 --> 00:06:58.484
-Yeah, I can't impress anybody,
nothing.

